{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016mTCtPyvyqFNQ7ZawE2h8A","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_3/projects/gen-depth-fingerprint/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Writing Plan — gen-depth-fingerprint\\\\n# Depth Fingerprinting of Recursive LLM Generation Chains\\\\n# Created: 2026-05-15\\\\n\\\\n##############################################################################\\\\n# 1. Submission Target\\\\n##############################################################################\\\\n\\\\nsubmission:\\\\n  primary:\\\\n    venue: EMNLP 2026 ARR\\\\n    deadline: 2026-05-25\\\\n    page_limit: \\\\\\\"8 pages (long) + unlimited appendix\\\\\\\"\\\\n    template: acl.sty\\\\n    special_requirements:\\\\n      - Limitations section (mandatory)\\\\n      - Ethics Statement\\\\n      - ARR submission format\\\\n    note: \\\\\\\"D012: 主投 EMNLP ARR，DDL 仅剩 10 天，全速推进\\\\\\\"\\\\n  fallback:\\\\n    - venue: AAAI 2027\\\\n      deadline: 2026-08-02\\\\n    - venue: ICLR 2027\\\\n      deadline: 2026-09-24\\\\n    - venue: NAACL 2027 ARR\\\\n      deadline: 2026-10-16\\\\n\\\\n##############################################################################\\\\n# 2. One-Sentence Contribution\\\\n##############################################################################\\\\n\\\\none_sentence: >\\\\n  We formulate ordinal depth estimation for recursive LLM generation chains,\\\\n  showing that distributional features exhibit differential depth response\\\\n  (central-tendency drifts, shape remains stationary), yielding a 7-feature\\\\n  ensemble that reliably classifies generation depth (LOGO F1=0.79) across\\\\n  6 generators / 3 model families (including 7B+ scale).\\\\n\\\\n##############################################################################\\\\n# 3. Claim-Evidence Map\\\\n##############################################################################\\\\n\\\\nclaims:\\\\n  C1_depth_discriminability:\\\\n    claim: >\\\\n      Distributional features under a held-out reference model classify\\\\n      generation depth (gen-0/gen-1/gen-2+) with macro-F1 significantly\\\\n      above chance, generalizing across unseen generators.\\\\n    evidence:\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-002-eval\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"LOGO avg macro-F1 = 0.8037\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-002-eval\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"Leave-one-family-out Δ = +0.0107 (Pythia vs non-Pythia)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-015-v2\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"Bootstrap CI [0.786, 0.799], p<0.001 vs all baselines\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-013\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"Length not a confound (|ρ|<0.14, normalized trends preserved)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-014\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"6-gen LOGO F1=0.7897 (incl. Qwen3-8B), held-out F1=0.6849, depth signal persists at 8B, cross-scale transfer gap noted\\\\\\\"\\\\n    tables: [Table 1, Table 2]\\\\n    figures: [Fig 2, Fig 3]\\\\n\\\\n  C2_differential_response:\\\\n    claim: >\\\\n      Central-tendency/diversity features (entropy_mean, TTR, hapax_ratio) drift\\\\n      monotonically with depth; shape features (entropy_std, tail_decay) remain\\\\n      near-stationary. Full 7-feature set significantly outperforms surface-only\\\\n      and reference-only subsets.\\\\n    evidence:\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-001-fix\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"full(0.82) > surface(0.76) > reference(0.72), CI non-overlapping\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-002\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"Drift direction consistent across all 6 generators (incl. 8B)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-002-eval\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"full(0.80) > ref(0.75) = surf(0.75), McNemar p≈0\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-003\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"3 cross-family ref models: LOGO F1 0.80-0.82, drift direction consistent\\\\\\\"\\\\n    tables: [Table 2]\\\\n    figures: [Fig 1]\\\\n\\\\n  C3_downstream_negative:\\\\n    claim: >\\\\n      Depth-aware data curation does NOT improve downstream CLM quality.\\\\n      Data quantity dominates depth composition. Depth fingerprinting is\\\\n      diagnostic, not curative.\\\\n    status: NEGATIVE FINDING — report honestly\\\\n    evidence:\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-004-v2\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"all(2.335) < size_matched(2.367) < depth01(2.387) ≈ binary_filtered(2.389)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-004-v2\\\\n        metric: \\\\\\\"15/15 runs, cross-seed variance <0.002\\\\\\\"\\\\n    tables: [Table 3]\\\\n    figures: [Fig 4]\\\\n    framing_note: >\\\\n      DO NOT hide or spin. Frame as: \\\\\\\"We tested whether depth-aware curation\\\\n      improves downstream quality. It does not. The primary determinant is data\\\\n      quantity, not depth composition. This positions depth fingerprinting as a\\\\n      diagnostic tool for provenance characterization, not a curative tool for\\\\n      data selection.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n##############################################################################\\\\n# 4. Paper Outline\\\\n##############################################################################\\\\n\\\\noutline:\\\\n  abstract:\\\\n    length: \\\\\\\"~200 words\\\\\\\"\\\\n    structure: \\\\\\\"five-sentence method (Farquhar)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_points:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"We formulate ordinal depth estimation beyond binary detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Why hard: existing detectors offer only real-vs-synthetic, no depth signal\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"How: 7 distributional features exhibiting differential depth response\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Evidence: LOGO F1=0.79 across 6 generators / 3 families (incl. 7B+), p<0.001 vs baselines\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Honest negative: depth-aware curation does not improve downstream quality\\\\\\\"\\\\n    headline_note: >\\\\n      The paper_framing.md headline template contains \\\\\\\"Z% downstream\\\\\\\" placeholder.\\\\n      UPDATE to negative-finding wording: \\\\\\\"...however, depth-aware data curation\\\\n      does not improve downstream model quality over random subsampling,\\\\n      positioning depth estimation as a diagnostic rather than curative tool.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    reviewer_concerns_covered: []\\\\n\\\\n  introduction:\\\\n    length: \\\\\\\"~1.5 pages\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_points:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem: web data increasingly contains recursive LLM-generated text of unknown provenance depth\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap: binary detectors cannot distinguish gen-1 from gen-2+, forcing all-or-nothing filtering\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Our formulation: ordinal depth estimation as a new task (genuinely novel)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Core finding: differential depth response — level/diversity features drift, shape features are stationary\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Practical consequence: 7-feature ensemble LOGO F1=0.79, reliable across unknown generators (incl. 7B+)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Honest reporting: downstream curation does not benefit (diagnostic, not curative)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Contributions list (3 items matching the 3 claims)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    evidence:\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-015-v2  # headline numbers\\\\n      - exp_id: plan-002-eval  # LOGO result\\\\n    reviewer_concerns_covered: [RC8]\\\\n    notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Must explicitly state contribution is empirical/conceptual, not methodological (D006+D007)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Connect to OOD detection literature in framing paragraph (RC8)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Do NOT overclaim 'dual dynamics' — use 'differential depth response' (D007)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  related_work:\\\\n    length: \\\\\\\"~1 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n    organization: # see literature_strategy section below\\\\n      - subsection: \\\\\\\"AI-Generated Text Detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n        papers: [detectgpt, gltr, dna_gpt, binoculars, fast_detectgpt, ld_score, intrinsic_dimension, diveye, generator_barrier, feat_aug_transformer, reliable_detection, paraphrase_evades, detection_possibilities, grover, release_strategies, jawahar_survey]\\\\n        angle: \\\\\\\"Binary detection only — no depth estimation capability. Single-score baselines show high cross-generator variance.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - subsection: \\\\\\\"Model Collapse and Iterative Generation\\\\\\\"\\\\n        papers: [self_consuming_mad, curse_of_recursion, strong_model_collapse, model_collapse_avoidable, broken_telephone, markovian_chains]\\\\n        angle: \\\\\\\"Training-loop collapse theory; iterative generation distortion. We study inference-chain depth without retraining.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - subsection: \\\\\\\"Vocabulary Diversity and Stylometry\\\\\\\"\\\\n        papers: [curious_decline, writing_diversity, nucleus_sampling, mapping_llm_science, monitoring_ai_review, stamatatos_survey, koppel_authorship, uchendu_attribution]\\\\n        angle: \\\\\\\"Diversity decline documented but not used for depth estimation. Our surface features are stylometric in nature.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - subsection: \\\\\\\"Data Quality and Provenance\\\\\\\"\\\\n        papers: [dsir, qurating, ccnet, watermark_llm, synthid_text, aaronson_watermark, chainwash, min_k_percent, ood_baseline]\\\\n        angle: \\\\\\\"Quality scoring/watermarking for data curation. Depth fingerprint complements these as provenance signal.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    reviewer_concerns_covered: [RC1, RC8]\\\\n\\\\n  method:\\\\n    length: \\\\\\\"~1.5 pages\\\\\\\"\\\\n    subsections:\\\\n      - name: \\\\\\\"Task Formulation\\\\\\\"\\\\n        content: \\\\\\\"Ordinal depth estimation: given text x, predict depth class {gen-0, gen-1, gen-2+}\\\\\\\"\\\\n        length: \\\\\\\"~0.25 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - name: \\\\\\\"Generation Chain Construction\\\\\\\"\\\\n        content: \\\\\\\"6 generators (Pythia-2.8B, Pythia-1B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3-1.7B, Qwen3-0.6B, Qwen3-8B), 3 families, ~1000 seeds × 5 depths, continuation prompt, temp=0.7/top_p=0.9/max_tokens=256\\\\\\\"\\\\n        evidence: [mvp-001, plan-002, plan-014]\\\\n        length: \\\\\\\"~0.25 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - name: \\\\\\\"Feature Extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n        content: \\\\\\\"7 features: 4 reference-model (entropy_mean/std/max, tail_decay) + 3 surface (TTR, hapax_ratio, entropy_min). Reference model = Pythia-410M.\\\\\\\"\\\\n        length: \\\\\\\"~0.5 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - name: \\\\\\\"Evaluation Protocol\\\\\\\"\\\\n        content: \\\\\\\"Leave-one-generator-out (LOGO) cross-validation. XGBoost classifier. Bootstrap CI (n=1000). McNemar test for feature ablation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n        length: \\\\\\\"~0.5 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n    reviewer_concerns_covered: [RC2, RC4, RC6]\\\\n\\\\n  results:\\\\n    length: \\\\\\\"~2 pages\\\\\\\"\\\\n    subsections:\\\\n      - name: \\\\\\\"Depth Classification Performance (C1)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        content: \\\\\\\"6-gen LOGO F1=0.79, per-generator breakdown (0.68-0.86), family-out Δ=+0.01. Gen-0 near-perfect (F1=0.95), gen-1 vs gen-2+ harder. Qwen3-8B held-out F1=0.6849 (cross-scale gap).\\\\\\\"\\\\n        evidence: [plan-002-eval, plan-015-v2, plan-014]\\\\n        tables: [Table 1]\\\\n        figures: [Fig 2]\\\\n        length: \\\\\\\"~0.5 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - name: \\\\\\\"Differential Depth Response (C2)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        content: \\\\\\\"Feature drift patterns. entropy_mean/TTR/hapax drift monotonically. entropy_std/tail_decay near-stationary. Feature complementarity: full > surface = reference.\\\\\\\"\\\\n        evidence: [plan-001-fix, plan-002, plan-003]\\\\n        tables: [Table 2]\\\\n        figures: [Fig 1]\\\\n        length: \\\\\\\"~0.5 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - name: \\\\\\\"Comparison with Detection Baselines\\\\\\\"\\\\n        content: \\\\\\\"7-feature vs Avg-LogProb (+3.9pp, p<0.001), FastDetectGPT (+6.7pp), LD-Score, Binoculars. Key advantage: tight CI vs high variance of single detectors.\\\\\\\"\\\\n        evidence: [plan-015-v2]\\\\n        figures: [Fig 3]\\\\n        length: \\\\\\\"~0.5 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - name: \\\\\\\"Downstream Utility — Negative Finding (C3)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        content: \\\\\\\"Depth-aware curation does not improve CLM quality. all(2.335) < size_matched(2.367) < depth01(2.387). Quantity dominates composition. Diagnostic not curative.\\\\\\\"\\\\n        evidence: [plan-004-v2]\\\\n        tables: [Table 3]\\\\n        figures: [Fig 4]\\\\n        length: \\\\\\\"~0.5 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n    reviewer_concerns_covered: [RC1, RC2, RC10, RC11]\\\\n\\\\n  discussion:\\\\n    length: \\\\\\\"~0.5 page\\\\\\\"\\\\n    key_points:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Why shape features are stationary: determined by sampling mechanism and architecture, invariant to input content drift (speculative, explicitly flagged)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Practical implications: risk-stratified data curation (flag gen-2+ for review, keep gen-1)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Honest framing of C3: negative finding has positive information value — rules out depth-based filtering as curation strategy\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Connection to model collapse literature: inference chains show similar distributional drift without retraining\\\\\\\"\\\\n    reviewer_concerns_covered: [RC3, RC8]\\\\n\\\\n  limitations:\\\\n    length: \\\\\\\"~0.25 page (mandatory for EMNLP; good practice for AAAI)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    items:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Generators up to 8B tested (plan-014); depth signal exists at scale but cross-scale transfer gap (8B held-out F1=0.685 vs ≤2.8B 0.76-0.86). Frontier models (70B+) untested.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Single prompt type (continuation); elaboration/rewriting chains not yet tested (plan-005 pending)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Lab-constructed single-model chains; real web contamination involves diverse generators per step\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Negative downstream result tested on CLM only; other downstream tasks not evaluated\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3-class granularity; finer-grained